"""Original source-linked writing; no fabricated expert review or affiliate claims."""
import json,re
from html import escape as e

def build(page,head,link,root):
 index=json.loads((root/'data/food-library/index.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
 examples=[]
 for identity,grams in [('fdc:171477',150),('fdc:168878',150),('fdc:171413',13.5),('fdc:170273',20),('fdc:170093',150)]:
  item=next(x for x in index if x['id']==identity)
  record=next(x for x in json.loads((root/('data/food-library/records/'+item['shard']+'.json')).read_text(encoding='utf-8')) if x['id']==identity)
  examples.append('<tr><th scope="row"><a href="/food-library.html?food='+identity+'">'+e(record['name'])+'</a><small>USDA SR Legacy, 2018 · '+str(grams)+' g</small></th>'+''.join('<td>'+('Unknown' if record['nutrients'][k] is None else str(round(record['nutrients'][k]*grams/100,1)))+'</td>' for k in ['cal','p','c','fat'])+'</tr>')
 # Extend useful writing at its established URL, preserving its published date and source discussion.
 path=root/'raw-vs-cooked-food-weight.html';text=path.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
 text=re.sub(r'<!-- library-examples:start -->.*?<!-- library-examples:end -->','',text,flags=re.S)
 addition='<section class="food-guide-section"><h2>Try an actual reference portion</h2><p>These are calculated examples from the final USDA SR Legacy edition, not measurements of your meal. The roasted chicken entry is breast meat only; the potato includes flesh and skin without salt. Olive oil is shown as a weighed 13.5 g portion, not a universal tablespoon conversion.</p><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Calculated source portions"><table><caption>Source amount per 100 g × example grams ÷ 100</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Food and weighed amount</th><th scope="col">kcal</th><th scope="col">Protein (g)</th><th scope="col">Carbs (g)</th><th scope="col">Fat (g)</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join(examples)+'</tbody></table></div><p>A source profile’s household measures apply only to that profile. Open a food to inspect the measures and full nutrient coverage, or include it in a <a href="/food-diary.html">private recipe</a>.</p><p>Foods from different source editions or preparations are not paired raw-and-cooked samples. Do not subtract their values to infer how your food changed during cooking.</p></section>'
 text=text.replace('<section class="resource-sources">','<!-- library-examples:start -->'+addition+'<!-- library-examples:end --><section class="resource-sources">',1)
 path.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
 sources={
  'nhs-vegan':'https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/how-to-eat-a-balanced-diet/the-vegan-diet/',
  'nhs-vegetarian':'https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/eat-well/how-to-eat-a-balanced-diet/the-vegetarian-diet/',
  'mediterranean':'https://www.heart.org/en/healthy-living/healthy-eating/eat-smart/nutrition-basics/mediterranean-diet',
  'dash':'https://www.nhlbi.nih.gov/health/dash/health-benefits',
  'carnivore':'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8684475/'}
 rows=[
  ('Vegan','Excludes animal foods. Plant-based is a broader label and does not necessarily mean vegan.','Use a reliable vitamin B12 source. Check fortified products rather than assuming all plant drinks contain the same nutrients.','NHS practical guidance describes planning for B12, calcium, iron, iodine and other nutrients.','nhs-vegan'),
  ('Vegetarian, flexitarian & plant-forward','Vegetarian patterns exclude meat and fish; flexitarian usually describes including them less often. Definitions of plant-forward vary.','Build meals from identifiable ingredients. A protein total does not show the full nutritional pattern.','NHS vegetarian guidance supports varied protein foods and attention to iron and B12. It does not certify every packaged vegetarian product.','nhs-vegetarian'),
  ('Mediterranean-style','A family of food patterns, not one fixed menu: vegetables, grains, legumes, nuts, olive oil and varying amounts of animal foods.','A recipe can fit the broad pattern with many different macro totals. Record the actual oil and portion.','The American Heart Association describes this pattern within its dietary guidance. A name on a restaurant menu is not evidence of the whole eating pattern.','mediterranean'),
  ('DASH','A structured eating pattern studied in controlled trials, with separate evidence about sodium reduction.','Use the official eating-plan resources for its food groups and serving framework. Our food notebook is not a treatment plan.','NHLBI describes randomized controlled DASH and DASH-Sodium studies. Their evidence is different from a self-selected online survey.','dash'),
  ('Carnivore','Commonly used for eating mostly or exclusively animal foods; individual definitions vary.','Do not infer safety, adequacy or disease treatment from a favorable anecdote or a protein number.','The 2021 survey of 2,029 self-selected participants reports their experiences. Self-report, selection effects and no randomized comparison limit causal conclusions and long-term safety claims.','carnivore')]
 body='<article class="food-app food-reading">'+head('Diet names are a starting point.','Compare what an eating pattern includes, what its evidence can tell you, and what a food log cannot.')+'<p>The ingredient, portion and overall pattern matter more than a label. This is an evidence-reading guide, not a prescription or a ranking.</p><p class="table-scroll-note">Scroll across to read the questions and source evidence.</p><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Diet definitions and evidence"><table><caption>Definitions, practical questions and source limits</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Pattern</th><th scope="col">What the label means</th><th scope="col">Question to ask</th><th scope="col">Evidence and source</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr><th scope="row">'+e(a)+'</th><td>'+e(b)+'</td><td>'+e(c)+'</td><td>'+e(d)+' <a href="'+sources[k]+'">Read source</a></td></tr>' for a,b,c,d,k in rows)+'</tbody></table></div><section class="food-guide-section"><h2>Animal-based and lower-carbohydrate labels</h2><p>“Animal-based” has no single standardized recipe or nutrient target. Ask what it includes before treating it as a comparable intervention. “Lower carbohydrate” also requires a stated amount and context; it should not automatically be read as ketogenic or as a disease-treatment recommendation.</p><p>For either label, examine the foods actually eaten, the comparison diet, study duration and outcomes. An isolated nutrient total cannot establish overall adequacy or a health effect.</p><h2>How to read a diet claim</h2><ol><li>Identify the study design: anecdote, survey, observational study, controlled trial or clinical guidance.</li><li>Check who participated and how they were selected.</li><li>Separate reported satisfaction from measured clinical outcomes.</li><li>Check duration, missing data, funding and whether the result applies to your situation.</li></ol><h2>Use the notebook without turning it into a grade</h2><p>Compare actual portions and recipes in the <a href="/food-library.html">food library</a>. Missing micronutrient fields do not show a deficiency, and one logged day does not define a dietary pattern.</p><p>Content sources inspected October 11, 2026. No clinician or dietitian review has been performed for this page. Individual medical decisions, restrictive diets, pregnancy and nutrition for children require appropriate professional guidance.</p></section>'+link('/food-diary.html','Check a portion')+'</article>'
 page('/diet-patterns-evidence.html','Vegan, Mediterranean, DASH & carnivore: definitions and evidence','Compare common diet labels, food patterns and evidence quality. See why a carnivore survey differs from controlled DASH trials and what food logging cannot establish.',body,'article')
 resources=[
  ('Read','Salt, Fat, Acid, Heat','Samin Nosrat, illustrated by Wendy MacNaughton. Publisher edition: April 25, 2017.','A practical cooking framework for understanding seasoning, texture and heat. Useful when learning how ingredients shape a recipe; it is not a macro database or clinical nutrition guide.','https://www.simonandschuster.net/books/Salt-Fat-Acid-Heat/Samin-Nosrat/9781476753836','Publisher and edition'),
  ('Watch / transcript','NOVA: The Truth About Fat','PBS / NOVA, 2020.','A science-documentary perspective on fat biology. Read claims in their research context. The official episode page currently says online streaming is unavailable; access depends on platform and region.','https://www.pbs.org/wgbh/nova/video/the-truth-about-fat/','Official episode archive'),
  ('Read','DASH eating-plan resources','U.S. National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute.','Free explanations of a studied dietary pattern and its research background. A useful starting point for understanding the source evidence, rather than choosing a diet from a social-media headline.','https://www.nhlbi.nih.gov/health/dash','Official resource collection')]
 body='<section class="food-app food-reading">'+head('A little more food for thought.','Cooking, science and evidence—each useful for a different reason.')+'<div class="food-source-list">'+''.join('<article><p>'+a+'</p><h2>'+b+'</h2><p>'+c+'</p><p>'+d+'</p><a href="'+url+'">'+label+' →</a></article>' for a,b,c,d,url,label in resources)+'</div><section class="food-guide-section"><h2>How this shelf is chosen</h2><p>Resources are checked against their creator, publisher or public institution. These summaries are original and based on the official descriptions; they do not claim firsthand testing, professional endorsement or independent review of every claim.</p><p>No affiliate links or sponsored placement are used on this page. We do not rank resources by popularity. Streaming and edition availability can change. Covers and video artwork are not reproduced.</p><p>Official pages inspected October 11, 2026. More books and creators will be added after their editions, source practices and relevant limitations are checked.</p></section>'+link('/diet-patterns-evidence.html','Reading diet evidence')+'</section>'
 page('/read-and-watch.html','Nutrition books, documentaries & useful reading','Explore a restrained, source-checked shelf of cooking and nutrition resources, with edition details, perspective, limits and honest streaming availability.',body,'editorial')
